{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And in the greatness of Your majesty.</b> Meaning: since He mentioned that His adversaries are terrified, He added to say that there is yet more for them — that He will destroy them with the greatness of His majesty. The intention is that He will not destroy them with a light destruction without commotion, but rather through wonders and signs He will execute upon them a written judgment. And His saying <b>You send forth Your wrath, it consumes them like stubble</b> — meaning: not that You need the greatness of Your majesty to destroy them, but rather even so, You are able to send forth a single wrath of Yours and they will be consumed like stubble."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:19.757998973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}